                "Grain_Size_Units": "",
                "Microstructural_Features": "well adhered to the substrate and, despite the presence of noncontinuous cracks, reasonably compact. remarkable deformation of particles. exhibit the presence of two distinct phase structures, the main lamellar MAX phase from Ti2AlC and some Ti3AlC2, and a titanium aluminide. some cracks parallel to the substrate. MAX exhibits a metal-like behaviour incase of relatively low impact velocity (Al2) with a deformation of particles during the impact. Neither debris nor fragmentation during spray is observed. No MAX-phase deterioration or coating oxidation"
            },
            "Notes": "Al2. Composition given for substrates was only partial, noted Bal. other."
